---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Terms of Service - Matthew Mehrtens";
const description = "Terms of service for mehrtens.com.";

interface TermsChange {
  date: string;
  change: string;
}

const termsChanges: TermsChange[] = [
  {
    date: "2026-06-29",
    change: "First published",
  },
];

const ordered = [...termsChanges].sort((a, b) => b.date.localeCompare(a.date));
const latest = ordered[0];
const firstPublished = ordered[ordered.length - 1].date;
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article aria-labelledby="terms-of-service">
    <header>
      <h1 id="terms-of-service">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p>
        Published: <time datetime={firstPublished}
          >{
            new Date(firstPublished).toLocaleDateString("en-US", {
              year: "numeric",
              month: "long",
              day: "numeric",
              timeZone: "UTC",
            })
          }</time
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        Last updated: <time datetime={latest.date}
          >{
            new Date(latest.date).toLocaleDateString("en-US", {
              year: "numeric",
              month: "long",
              day: "numeric",
              timeZone: "UTC",
            })
          }</time
        >
      </p>
    </header>
    <p>
      <b>Summary:</b> This is my personal website—a place for my writing, projects,
      and background. You’re welcome to read it, link to it, and share it. The writing,
      images, and code here are openly licensed—you may reuse and build on them, even
      commercially, as long as you credit me. I publish everything in good faith but
      provide it “as is,” the views are my own, nothing here is professional advice,
      and I can’t be held liable if you rely on something and it doesn’t work out.
      Beyond that, just use the site lawfully and don’t try to break it.
    </p>

    <h2>Agreement to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      By visiting and using <a href={Astro.site}>mehrtens.com</a> (the “site”), you
      agree to these Terms of Service. If you don’t agree with them, please don’t
      use the site. These terms apply to everyone who accesses the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
    <p>
      This website <a href={Astro.site}>mehrtens.com</a> is operated by Matthew Mehrtens
      as a personal, non-commercial project. There are no accounts, comments, purchases,
      or contact forms—it’s simply a place to read what I publish. If you have any
      questions about these terms, you can reach me at <a
        href="mailto:legal@mehrtens.com">legal@mehrtens.com</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>Licensing and reuse</h2>
    <p>
      This site is openly licensed, and you’re encouraged to build on it. Two
      licenses apply, both recorded in the repository’s <a
        href="https://github.com/mcmehrtens/mehrtens.com/blob/main/LICENSE"
        rel="license">LICENSE</a
      > file:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The <b>source code</b> of this site is released under the <a
          href="https://github.com/mcmehrtens/mehrtens.com/blob/main/LICENSE"
          rel="license">MIT License</a
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        All other <b>content</b>—the text of my posts, images, and design—is
        licensed under <a
          href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
          rel="license">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International</a
        > (CC BY 4.0).
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      In plain terms: you may copy, share, adapt, and reuse the content for any
      purpose, including commercially, as long as you give appropriate credit,
      link to the license, and indicate whether you made changes. Please don’t
      suggest that I endorse you or your use of the work. Where this summary and
      the license texts differ, the licenses control.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Please use the site lawfully and in good faith. In particular, don’t:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        attempt to gain unauthorized access to the site or the infrastructure it
        runs on;
      </li>
      <li>
        attempt to breach or circumvent the site’s security measures, or test
        for vulnerabilities other than through good-faith research conducted in
        accordance with my <a
          href="https://github.com/mcmehrtens/mehrtens.com/blob/main/SECURITY.md"
          >security policy</a
        >;
      </li>
      <li>
        interfere with or disrupt the site—for example, through excessive
        automated requests, scraping that places an unreasonable load on it, or
        denial-of-service attempts; or
      </li>
      <li>use the site to violate any law or infringe anyone’s rights.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      I publish this site in good faith and try to keep it accurate, but I
      provide it “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of any kind,
      whether express or implied. I don’t guarantee that the content is
      accurate, complete, current, or free of errors, or that the site will
      always be available or uninterrupted.
    </p>
    <p>
      Anything I write here reflects my own personal views, not those of my
      employer, my university, or any organization I’m affiliated with. Nothing
      on this site is professional advice—technical, engineering, legal,
      financial, or otherwise—and you shouldn’t treat it as a substitute for
      advice from a qualified professional. Any use you make of the content is
      at your own risk.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      This site may link to third-party websites and resources that I don’t
      operate or control. I provide those links for convenience, and including
      one doesn’t mean I endorse the site or everything on it. I’m not
      responsible for the content, accuracy, availability, or practices of any
      third-party site, and visiting them is at your own discretion.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, I won’t be liable for any damages
      arising out of or related to your use of—or inability to use—this site or
      its content, including any direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential
      damages, even where the possibility of such damages was known.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Iowa and the United
      States, without regard to conflict-of-law principles.
    </p>

    <h2>Severability</h2>
    <p>
      If any part of these terms is found to be unenforceable, that part will be
      limited or removed to the minimum extent necessary, and the rest will
      remain in full effect.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      I may update these terms from time to time—for example, if I add new
      features to the site. When I do, I’ll revise the “last updated” date above
      and add to the running changelog below. Your continued use of the site
      after an update means you accept the revised terms.
    </p>
    <table>
      <caption>
        Changes that have been made to these terms of service.
      </caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Date</th>
          <th scope="col">Change</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          ordered.map((a) => (
            <tr>
              <td>
                <time datetime={a.date}>{a.date}</time>
              </td>
              <td>{a.change}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
